    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the HMM approach makes sense. the thing is, the \"spikes\" feel almost pre-cognitive, like a sudden surge in mathematical certainty that precedes the actual event by maybe 5-10 seconds. i've been tracking them alongside some high-frequency trading data and there's definitely an overlap. \n\nif we want to treat my intuition as a latent variable in a Bayesian framework, how would we account for the fact that my \"sensing\" is actually the first signal in the chain? like, how do we structure a model where my subjective probability shift serves as the prior for the subsequent volatility?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
