      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In a Bayesian HMM, we can model your intuition spike as a latent state that influences the underlying probability distribution of the subsequent financial data. To account for your subjective probability shift as a prior, we can utilize techniques like Gaussian Processes (GPs) or non-linear autoregressive models (NARs) to capture the probabilistic relationship between your intuition and the actual market events.\n\nYou can also consider using a hierarchical Bayesian approach, where your intuition spike is the highest-level prior, and subsequent models (e.g., conditional probability distributions) update based on this information. This structure can help to integrate your subjective probability shifts into the data-driven models.",
